-- title:
--   Kernel of [p]^* equals kernel of the transition map
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $h$ a natural number, and let $A$ be a family of commutative rings $A_w$, indexed by $w \in \mathbb{N}$, each carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose comultiplication is cocommutative and which is finite as a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-module. Suppose given, for each $w$, a map $t_w : A_{w+1} \to A_w$ that is simultaneously an algebra and a coalgebra homomorphism over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, such that: each $t_w$ is surjective; $\dim_{\mathbb{Z}/p} A_w = p^{wh}$ for all $w$; and for each $w$ the kernel of $t_w$ equals the $p^w$-torsion ideal of $A_{w+1}$, that is, the ideal generated by the image, under the $p^w$-th convolution power $\mathrm{nsmulAlgHom}$ of the identity of $A_{w+1}$, of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\varepsilon)$. Then for every $v$ and every $a \in A_{v+1}$ one has $\mathrm{nsmulAlgHom}(p)(a) = 0$ if and only if $t_v(a) = 0$: the kernel of the $p$-th convolution power of the identity on $A_{v+1}$ coincides with the kernel of the transition map $t_v$.
--
--   For a $p$-divisible group over $\mathbb{F}_p$ presented as a tower of finite cocommutative Hopf algebras, this is the assertion that multiplication by $p$ on the $(v+1)$-st level is, on the level of coordinate rings, the transition map $t_v$ up to an injection — equivalently that $[p] : G_{v+1} \to G_v$ is an epimorphism. It is used in the project's Frobenius–Verschiebung cancellation arguments, notably by [`PDivisibleGroup.Tower.eq_of_frobenius_comp_eq_zmodp`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.Tower.eq_of_frobenius_comp_eq_zmodp).
